   "source": [
    "## 6. Common exception types\n",
    "\n",
    "Here are some exception types that appear often in beginner Python programs.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3e946ebe",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "e7abe16a"
   },
   "source": [
    "| Type | Reason exception is raised |\n",
    "| :--------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n",
    "| `EOFError` | `input()` hits an end-of-file condition (EOF) without reading any input. |\n",
    "| `KeyError` | A dictionary key is not found in the set of keys. |\n",
    "| `ZeroDivisionError` | Divide by zero error |\n",
    "| `ValueError` | Invalid value (Ex: Input mismatch) |\n",
    "| `IndexError` | Index is out of bounds. |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d36d779f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Multiple exception handlers\n",
    "\n",
    "A `try` block may raise different kinds of exceptions.\n",
    "In that case, we can use multiple `except` blocks and handle each error differently.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Handy example\n",
    "Try the following cases:\n",
    "- enter a valid number\n",
    "- enter `0`\n",
    "- enter text such as `hello`\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "526dc1c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "while True:\n",
    "    num1 = 12\n",
    "    num2_input = input(\"Enter the second number (or 'done' to quit): \")\n",
    "\n",
    "    if num2_input.lower() in ('done', 'quit'):\n",
    "        print(\"Exiting calculation.\")\n",
    "        break\n",
    "\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        num2 = float(num2_input)\n",
    "        result = num1 / num2\n",
    "        print(f\"Result: {result}\")\n",
    "    except ValueError:\n",
    "        print(\"Invalid input. Please enter a valid number.\")\n",
    "    except ZeroDivisionError:\n",
    "        print(\"You cannot divide by zero.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1f521e5c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Raising exceptions with `raise`\n",
    "\n",
    "Sometimes Python does not automatically know that a value is logically invalid.\n",
    "For example, a negative number may be a valid number type, but still be invalid for your program.\n",
    "\n",
    "In such cases, we can raise an exception ourselves.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7a65bc5a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "age = int(input(\"Enter your age: \"))\n",
    "\n",
    "if age < 0:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Age cannot be negative.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Age is valid:\", age)\n"
   ]
  },
